- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/staff-domain/abroad
  route: staff-domain/abroad
  key: abroad
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:Circumstance
  label: Absence abroad
  definition: Temporary absence from Great Britain, permanent residence abroad and exportability are separate
    benefit-specific questions; duration, purpose, destination and dates matter. Overseas wording identifies
    a research topic, not an applicable rule or a benefit. Great Britain and the United Kingdom are not
    interchangeable territorial tests. Domestic temporary absence and a holiday without a stated destination
    do not establish travel abroad. The linked SPC branch concerns Pension Credit only; it does not establish
    rules for JSA, ESA, PIP, Universal Credit, State Pension or all benefits.
  aliases:
  - abroad
  - moves abroad
  - go abroad
  - overseas
  - travel abroad
  - travel overseas
  - living abroad
  - living overseas
  - outside Great Britain
  - outside GB
  source_candidates:
  - source-c001
  - source-c002
  review_status: unreviewed-specialist-review-required
- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/term/intl-spc-claimant-absence
  route: term/intl-spc-claimant-absence
  key: intl-spc-claimant-absence
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:DecisionRule
  label: SPC claimant temporary absence in the source
  definition: Source-bounded Pension Credit research through DMG 077001–077004, not a rule for all
    benefits. Other entitlement conditions must continue. The captured four-week branch requires an
    absence not expected to exceed four weeks; the examples distinguish expected duration from an
    early return or later extension. The eight-week branch requires the specified death connection, an
    absence not expected to exceed eight weeks and the Secretary of State considering return within
    four weeks unreasonable. The twenty-six-week branch requires an absence not expected to exceed
    twenty-six weeks and solely for the specified treatment, medically approved convalescence or care,
    or accompanying the specified person. Preserve the practitioner, pre-existing-condition and
    accompanying-person qualifications exactly as stated on pages 9–11; being abroad when an accident
    occurs is not itself the stated purpose condition. The qualified-practitioner definition continues
    onto page 11. Household membership, qualifying young person, the dated 2016 transition and the
    source-described non-export boundary need separate conditional review. Destination, purpose,
    expected and actual duration, relevant date and household facts remain unknown. Statutory
    reconciliation and the DMG 04642 supersession cross-reference remain open.
  aliases: []
  source_candidates: []
  additional_sources:
  - family: dmg
    document_id: dmg-vol2-ch7-part6
    page: 8
    anchor: '077001'
  - family: dmg
    document_id: dmg-vol2-ch7-part6
    page: 9
    anchor: '077002'
  - family: dmg
    document_id: dmg-vol2-ch7-part6
    page: 10
    anchor: '077004'
  - family: dmg
    document_id: dmg-vol2-ch7-part6
    page: 11
    anchor: form of treatment
  required_source_ids:
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part6/0008
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part6/0009
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part6/0010
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part6/0011
  required_concepts:
  - intl-spc-household-absence
  - intl-spc-absence-transition-2016
  - intl-spc-non-export
  review_status: unreviewed-specialist-review-required
- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/term/intl-spc-household-absence
  route: term/intl-spc-household-absence
  key: intl-spc-household-absence
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:DecisionRule
  label: SPC household membership during temporary absence
  definition: DMG 077005–077007 describe when a temporarily absent person is treated as a member of
    the claimant’s household. This is a separate question from the claimant-payment provision at
    077001. Keep the household branch’s own expected-duration, specified death connection, Secretary
    of State reasonableness and sole-purpose treatment/accompanying conditions; the twenty-six-week
    provision continues onto page 12. Do not transfer the claimant’s list of people or invent
    household facts. Where a qualifying young person matters, DMG 077008–077014 span pages 12–13,
    including education/training, age, continuity and benefit-receipt qualifications and references to
    ADM E2092/F1093. Those cross-references and current legal applicability remain unreconciled.
  aliases: []
  source_candidates: []
  additional_sources:
