  route: term/intl-spc-non-export
  key: intl-spc-non-export
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:DecisionRule
  label: SPC non-export in the cited EC classification
  definition: DMG 077025 describes SPC as a special non-contributory benefit in its cited EC-law
    classification and distinguishes payment in the state of habitual residence from export to
    claimants living abroad. Its citation continues onto page 14. DMG 077026 states that SPC is
    outside the reciprocal agreements described there. Keep the source’s regime, territory and date
    limits; no post-exit or present-day legal applicability is established by this classification. The
    adjacent overseas-resident State Pension provisions beginning at 077027 concern a different
    benefit and must not be treated as Pension Credit rules.
