- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/staff-domain/household-separation
  route: staff-domain/household-separation
  key: household-separation
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:Circumstance
  label: Pension Credit household separation and care-home residence
  definition: DMG 77013 defines a couple; DMG 77102 explains household as a domestic establishment, not merely
    a building. Under DMG 77128, one partner entering a care home permanently is treated as no longer in the
    same household. Where both enter permanently, the decision maker must establish whether they remain one
    household on the facts. DMG 77129–77130 require reasonable independence and responsibility in running a
    domestic establishment; the seven factors are non-exhaustive and none is decisive alone. DMG 78089 says
    each may claim when household membership ends, not that an award automatically follows. Temporary absence
    is a separate branch.
  aliases:
  - household separation
  - both partners in a care home
  source_candidates:
  - source-c010
  - source-c028
  required_source_ids:
