- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/staff-domain/mixed-age-pension-credit
  route: staff-domain/mixed-age-pension-credit
  key: mixed-age-pension-credit
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:Applicability
  label: Pension Credit mixed-age couple conditions and protections
  definition: 'DMG 77035 distinguishes new claims from 15 May 2019 and continuity protection linked to Pension Credit
    or pension-age Housing Benefit on 14 May 2019. DMG 77140–77184 distinguish the mixed-age definition, Universal
    Credit interaction, excluded-partner exceptions and effective dates. The general exclusion is not the complete
    rule. DMG memo 04/24 paragraphs 15–17 add a protected mixed-age migration route from 8 June 2024: the specified
    protected couples sent a migration notice may reclaim pension-age Housing Benefit or claim Pension Credit within
    three months after the relevant UC or HB award ends. That route requires its stated prior entitlement and migration
    facts; it is not a general right for every mixed-age couple. Contemporary applicability, legislation and the
    ADM counterpart still require reconciliation.'
  aliases:
  - mixed-age couple
  - mixed age couple
  - protected mixed-age couple
  source_candidates:
