- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/staff-domain/severe-disability-ignored-persons
  route: staff-domain/severe-disability-ignored-persons
  key: severe-disability-ignored-persons
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:Applicability
  label: People whose presence is ignored for the Pension Credit disability addition
  definition: 'A limited disregard for the residence condition of the Pension Credit severe-disability additional
    amount, not a finding that a person is absent from the household for every purpose. Assess normal residence
    separately. The captured DMG 78077 categories are: a person aged under 18; a person receiving source-defined
    “AA”, highest- or middle-rate DLA care, standard- or enhanced-rate PIP or ADP daily living, or AFIP; a
    person certified as blind or severely sight impaired by a consultant ophthalmologist or treated as such;
    a person living with the claimant to care for the claimant or partner who is engaged by a charitable or
    voluntary organisation which charges the claimant or partner for their services; that carer’s partner;
    and a source-defined qualifying young person, or a child for Child Benefit purposes. DMG 78008 limits treated blindness
    to 28 weeks after regained eyesight and no longer being certified. A voluntary organisation is non-profit
    and is not a public authority or local authority. Named young-person definitions have age, education,
    training, benefit-receipt and interruption conditions; neither education alone nor being under 20 is enough.
    DMG 78078(1) requires first joining the household to care for the claimant or partner, with the claimant
    or partner satisfying the additional-amount conditions immediately beforehand, and applies only for the
    first 12 weeks after joining. Its commercial-payment route concerns a person who is not a close relative:
    payment liability runs either from that person to the claimant or partner for occupation of their dwelling,
    or from the claimant or partner to that person for occupation of that person’s dwelling; it also covers
    membership of that person’s household. DMG 78079 requires legal liability and a payment broadly comparable
    to a lodger’s similar accommodation and facilities. The joint-occupation route requires co-ownership or
    joint liability to the same landlord, with its non-close-relative condition and the person’s-partner branch.
    The close-relative exception requires satisfying DMG 78078(3) or (4) as well as the timing condition:
    the claimant or partner’s co-ownership or joint liability must have arisen before 11 April 1988 or,
    if later, on or before first occupation; the note uses the right-to-occupy
    date, not a later moving-in date. Close relative has the captured legal, adoptive and half-sibling meanings.
    DMG 78080’s registered shared-lives route must retain the accommodation/support and commercial licence
    conditions and the exclusion where other people cannot be ignored; its completed example is not a general
    award rule or a current rate. Memo 02/25 paragraph 15 adds Pension Age Disability Payment to the ignored-person
    benefit list from 21 October 2024, separately from the memo’s claimant/partner and housing-deduction propositions.
    The dated statutory paragraph 2 also contains Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance wording requiring
    separate legal reconciliation; this concept does not consolidate it. Receipt conditions need the full
    DMG 78060 continuation: its partner-patient item must not be transferred automatically to a third person.
    Residence, receipt and component, age, care arrangements, relationship, liability and relevant dates remain
    unknown until evidenced. No staff question establishes these facts or that this component is payable.'
  aliases:
  - people whose presence is ignored
  - ignored persons for the severe-disability addition
  source_candidates: []
  required_source_ids:
