- '@id': https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/staff-domain/severe-disability-normal-residence
  route: staff-domain/severe-disability-normal-residence
  key: severe-disability-normal-residence
  '@type':
  - skos:Concept
  - dwp:Applicability
  label: Normal residence and sharing accommodation for the disability addition
  definition: 'Source-bounded navigation through DMG 78065–78076, separate from ignoring a person’s presence
    under 78077–78080 and from deciding whether partners remain one household. Normal residence is where a
    person usually lives: exceptional visits or absences are disregarded, and temporary absence does not itself
    change the normal home. DMG 78067 requires factual consideration of time, frequency, permanence, intentions,
    circumstances, degree of sharing, services, other accommodation and liabilities. An address, university
    term or overnight stay alone does not settle that assessment. Sharing only a bathroom, lavatory or communal
    area, or separate legal payment liabilities to the same landlord, has the captured sharing exceptions.
    Kitchen sharing can exist without entering or using it when personal items are stored or meals prepared
    there; merely passing through to a self-contained flat is different. DMG 78072–78075 require the contractual
    capacity and intention to create legal relations, an obligation for occupation from a recognised source
    of law, and the stipulated connection between non-payment and ending the licence or lease; another liability
    to a third party is not the same-landlord condition. Retain the England-and-Wales scope and presumption
    in the captured capacity passage rather than infer incapacity from a diagnosis. For an overnight carer,
    establish the separate address, actual use and frequency, postal address and Council Tax registration.
    All residence and contractual facts remain unknown until evidenced. A finding about this residence condition
    is not a finding of benefit entitlement, ignored-person status or continuing couple membership.'
  aliases:
  - normal residence for the disability addition
  - sharing accommodation for the disability addition
  source_candidates: []
  required_source_ids:
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0017
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0018
  - https://chris-page-gov.github.io/okf-dwp/id/page/78/0019
